 "name": "S6: Ch3, Hiring",
 "text_content": "Pages 193 to 215. Chapter 3, Hiring.\n\nS\u014fn output (draft): role scorecards, interview loop, hiring decision process.\n\nHighest-leverage session in the program. S\u014fn hires a full FOH and BOH team through 2026. Every one of those hires runs through whatever this session builds.\n\nCoupling to log: whatever scorecard dimensions this session sets, the review rubric in Session 13 must score against the same dimensions. A hiring bar and a performance bar that measure different things will produce people who were hired correctly and reviewed unfairly.\n\nChef partner: her senior-hire material is relevant to the open chef partner seat. If that conversation accelerates, this session gets pulled forward out of sequence, and the cost of doing so without Session 2 complete gets stated plainly.",
 "description": "Pages 193 to 215. Chapter 3, Hiring.\n\nS\u014fn output (draft): role scorecards, interview loop, hiring decision process.\n\nHighest-leverage session in the program. S\u014fn hires a full FOH and BOH team through 2026. Every one of those hires runs through whatever this session builds.\n\nCoupling to log: whatever scorecard dimensions this session sets, the review rubric in Session 13 must score against the same dimensions. A hiring bar and a performance bar that measure different things will produce people who were hired correctly and reviewed unfairly.\n\nChef partner: her senior-hire material is relevant to the open chef partner seat. If that conversation accelerates, this session gets pulled forward out of sequence, and the cost of doing so without Session 2 complete gets stated plainly.",
 "markdown_description": "**Pages 193 to 215.** Chapter 3, Hiring.\n\n**S\u014fn output (draft):** role scorecards, interview loop, hiring decision process.\n\n**Highest-leverage session in the program.** S\u014fn hires a full FOH and BOH team through 2026. Every one of those hires runs through whatever this session builds.\n\n**Coupling to log:** whatever scorecard dimensions this session sets, the review rubric in Session 13 must score against the same dimensions. A hiring bar and a performance bar that measure different things will produce people who were hired correctly and reviewed unfairly.\n\n**Chef partner:** her senior-hire material is relevant to the open chef partner seat. If that conversation accelerates, this session gets pulled forward out of sequence, and the cost of doing so without Session 2 complete gets stated plainly.",
